Hi,

For a long time I've played "stupid" characters like barbarians and
valkyries.  I wanted to try new aspects of the game, so I've been playing
wizard for some time now.  Spells are a lot of fun, but my games never
last.  I rarely get below AC 5, so even at XP level 10 i'm losing hit
points fast.

I can't use most of the armor I'm used to from barbarians et al, since they
impact my spellcasting abilities.  I know I can wear anything leather, but
they're not so effective after all.  A couple of times I've been given
wishes by water demons, and I've gotten +3 and +4 silver dragon scale mail
which brought me well below AC 0.  That was great, but it's a little hard
to rely on water demons and quaffing fountains all the time :)  I can
always try to get a magic marker + blank scrolls + knowledge of enchant
armor, but I usually have to play a while to get all that, and it's in that
early period of a game that I'm most vulnerable.

What do you do to survive as a wizard?  Do you have to largely depend on
luck?

